# Firm Ontology Platform — environment template.
#
# STUB mode (default) needs NO .env at all — `make bootstrap` runs fully offline.
#
# FULL mode: copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. That is the ONLY
# value the containerized full stack needs — docker-compose.full.yml forces PROVIDER_MODE=full,
# EMBED_BACKEND=fastembed and NEO4J_URI=bolt://neo4j:7687 for you, and injects the key via env_file.
# The key is never baked into an image and never committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # then edit ANTHROPIC_API_KEY below
#   make bootstrap MODE=full

# ---- LLM (required for full mode) -----------------------------------------------------------
# A funded Anthropic API key. Full mode needs API credit on the SAME org as the key.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ---- Optional overrides ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host port the web UI binds to (container serves on :80 internally).
# WEB_PORT=5173
# Neo4j host ports (Browser / Bolt) for poking at the graph directly.
# NEO4J_HTTP_PORT=7474
# NEO4J_BOLT_PORT=7687
# Routing profile: balanced (Sonnet 5 heavy / Haiku 4.5 light) | quality-max (Opus 5 heavy).
# ROUTING_PROFILE=balanced
# EDGAR requires a declared User-Agent ("Name email") for real filing pulls in full mode.
# EDGAR_USER_AGENT=Your Name your.email@example.com

# ---- Prebuilt images (GHCR) — only for docker-compose.prebuilt.yml --------------------------
# REGISTRY=ghcr.io/<owner>
# IMAGE_TAG=v0.1.0

# ---- Host/dev mode only (NOT used by the container stack) ------------------------------------
# The compose stack sets these itself; they matter only if you run uvicorn on the host.
# PROVIDER_MODE=stub
# EMBED_BACKEND=hash
# NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687
# NEO4J_USER=neo4j
# NEO4J_PASSWORD=firmontology
# SQLITE_PATH=./data/app.db
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
